{
  "out": "/tmp/photonz-playtest/a-recording-replaced-while-open-reloads-walk",
  "seed": "A recording is open, scrubbed and played, and its file is swapped on disk under the window: once written over in place, once by a new file taking its place. The window takes on the new file by itself with the playhead where it was, unedited, and nothing of the old file is ever shown scrubbing back or forth. Then an edited one: its cut and its place stay, and undoing the cut does not bring the old file back. On 2026-11-24, before this, 26 of 91 pictures scrubbing backwards were the old file's until the person pressed play.",
  "setup": { "timelineOpen": true, "history": 4, "forget": ["all"] },
  "steps": [
